    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "SETS\n\nA set holds each value at most once. Insert the same tag twice and it is still stored once.\nSet nodes (Hashset Insert / Contains / Union / Intersection) take and return a set, so chain them\nalong a wire.\nClass variables hold single values (numbers, text, booleans), so the collection itself lives on the wires between nodes and only the answers are stored in variables.",
